Brand setup and posting: see `brand.py` and `publish.py`. Brand files, posts, data and renders live in `brands/<slug>/`, so older paths below mean that folder.

# Falcon (FocusComet content engine)

Working name Falcon. Current state and next steps: `../HANDOVER.md`.

A self-run version of what Fastlane does: find what already works, copy the format (never the words or media),
write a FocusComet version, check it, render it for Instagram and TikTok, and queue it for review.

## Use it
    cd reels-pipeline/content-engine
    ../.venv/bin/python server.py            # dashboard at http://localhost:8787
    ../.venv/bin/python run.py daily --n 2   # the daily run: refresh, write 2 posts, gate, render

Dashboard tabs: **Planned posts** (status, scores, IG/TikTok slides, caption, Approve/Skip/Rework),
**Competitor ads** (longest-running active ads, Remix), **Trending** (this week's outlier posts as live Instagram
embeds, Remix). **Refresh** re-pulls tabs 2 and 3; **Make 2 posts** does the full daily run.

## Pipeline
| step | file | what |
|---|---|---|
| find | find.py, seeds.json | outlier Reels (views / account median) and carousels/images ((likes + 4 x comments) / account median) from seed accounts, Instagram Graph API; political posts skipped |
| tiktok | tiktok.py | this week's top US TikTok hashtags across ALL categories (Discovery API), their top videos, and a Sonnet judge (from video frames) on whether FocusComet can join each trend (fit, brand safety, our version). TikTok blocks downloads from the terminal, so Claude captures frames in Chrome for the judge |
| engagement | engagement.py | reposts (Instagram) and saves + shares (TikTok) read from public pages in Chrome during a session; trending is re-ranked by share rate |
| calendar | calendar_plan.py | ready posts into 12:30pm / 7:30pm ET slots: one per angle group a week, no format twice in a row, videos in the evening |
| competitors | competitors.py | competitor ads by days running (Ad Library); top 20 videos kept in data/ad_media via yt-dlp |
| write | write.py, brand.md, llm.py | Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude -p`, Mit's subscription) writes from a source; brand.md is the only source of facts; Claude Sonnet 5.5 judges |
| gate | gate.py | hook >= 62, human >= 70, banned claims, slide length, and a Sonnet judge (sounds human, clear, claims true, save/share >= 7). A post whose angle repeats one in the review queue (ready/approved, last 14 days) fails too. Fails are rewritten up to 3 times, else "held" with reasons |
| photos | photos.py | Pixabay (real stock first), picked per slide by Sonnet; Pexels by hand via Chrome |
| render | render.py | HyperFrames: essay, tweet, statement, quote, slideshow, caption; 1080x1350 and --tiktok 1080x1920 |

Nothing is posted. "ready" means it passed every check and waits for Mit.

## Added 10 Nov 2026: daily trends, three more platforms, installs without tracked links

**Daily trends (`trends.py`, Discovery tab > Today's trends).** find.py ranks a post against its own account over its
last 30 posts, so age doesn't count. trends.py ranks by engagement gained **per hour** over the last 72 hours, so this
morning's post beats last month's bigger one. Sources: the seed accounts, Instagram hashtag top posts (4 tags a day from
`trend_hashtags`; Meta allows 30 a week) and YouTube Shorts (`trend_queries`, `trend_countries`). Shares aren't public on
Instagram or YouTube, so they're estimated from likes until a real count is read in Chrome (engagement.json). Sonnet
reads the top 8 (at most 4 from YouTube). Reworked 11-12 Nov with Mit, three models with three jobs: **Sonnet** reads
each video (format, beats, mechanism, AI risk, a fit score as advice); **ChatGPT** (the Codex CLI, `llm.ask_chatgpt`)
writes five different scripts for each of the best 4, bound only by brand.md, writing.md and the gate's claims rule
(`gate.CLAIMS_RULE`: bold claims and a character's own first-person results are allowed); **Opus** hands Mit the best
two with reasons. Nothing is auto-rejected: on the dashboard Mit presses Reject or Use this per script, and Use this
sends that script to the writer as its direction. Sources are relevant people only: `seed_accounts` (22 study,
productivity and digital-wellbeing accounts, verified readable 12 Nov; the old list is `seed_accounts_before_1111`),
`trend_hashtags` (26), `trend_channels` (16 YouTube channels, about 3 quota units each) and `trend_queries`.
`trends.py blueprint <id>` writes a shot-by-shot plan
(measured cuts, each shot's job, and the lowest-risk way to make it: screen recording, stock, text card, then Hypit)
into `work/trends/<id>/BLUEPRINT.md`. It starts no paid generation.

**Meta's hourly budget.** One full pull of the seed accounts and hashtags used 76% of the app's hourly call budget on 11 Nov, and the scheduler
shares that budget. `igapi.discover` now caches for an hour, never waits on a limit and stops at 60%. Don't run
find.py or trends.py several times in one hour: on 10 Nov three test runs used all of it and one scheduler run failed.

**LinkedIn, Threads and X (`social.py`, Social tab).** Text-first posts written natively for each, in
`brands/<slug>/social/`. `social.py write` drafts the open slots (one Opus call and one Sonnet fact check per platform);
Approve schedules a post; the scheduler runs `social.py due --go`. A platform stays idle until its keys are in the
credentials file (empty lines are already there) and its handle or author id is in brand.json under `social`, which is
what stops a post reaching the wrong account. LinkedIn and X are written in the founder's voice from
`brands/<slug>/founder.md` (the only personal facts the writer may use); Threads is the brand account. After adding
keys: `social.py health`, then `deploy.py secrets`. Never tested against the live APIs: no keys existed on 10 Nov.

**Installs without per-post links (`insights.py`).** One bio link serves the whole account, so each post gets two
numbers instead: `keyword_comments` (people who commented HIDE, counted from the post's comments) and `est_link_taps`
(the day's bio-link taps from Instagram's account insights, split between the posts live that day by reach; an
estimate). Their sum is `intent`, printed by `insights.py` as a ranking. Not yet run against live data.

## Keys (reels-pipeline/.env)
META_IG_TOKEN (Instagram Graph API, long-lived, expires ~late Dec 2026), PIXABAY_KEY, TIKTOK_APP_ID and TIKTOK_APP_SECRET (pasted by Mit), TIKTOK_TOKEN and TIKTOK_ADVERTISER_ID (written by `tiktok.py auth` or the dashboard's /tiktok/callback). Gemini is reserved for Omni video generation; the engine itself uses only Claude (Opus writes, Sonnet judges). The writer uses the Claude subscription via the `claude` CLI, so it counts against plan usage.

## Known limits
- Competitor ads refresh automatically only after Mit's one-time ID check (facebook.com/ID) unlocks the Ad Library
  API; until then they are collected in Claude's session.
- TikTok's Discovery API gives trending hashtags and video links, not counts; saves/shares come from the Chrome pass, which needs a Claude session. Posting needs app review; TikTok versions are for manual upload.
- Instagram never shows other accounts' saves or shares (API or web). Reposts are the public share signal.
- No check here predicts views. Real results (saves, shares, reach) should replace the gate's judgment over time.
